EMP-PY 2.0.5 (unreleased)

Results on valid input do not change. On 6,018 test cases, version 2.0.5 gives
the same EMPC, EMP, MP and fraction values as version 2.0.4, bit for bit.

Bug fixes

* The ROC convex hull no longer uses scipy.spatial.ConvexHull. That function
  raised QhullError when the ROC curve had fewer than three points or when all
  its points lay on one line, for example with constant scores or a diagonal
  ROC curve with ties. A monotone-chain hull replaces it. The hull is computed
  on the integer counts of false and true positives, so the test for collinear
  points is exact.
* Invalid input raises ValueError. Version 2.0.4 called sys.exit, which ended
  the Python process.
* A sample with only one class raises a ValueError that names the problem.
  Version 2.0.4 failed with "ValueError: Points cannot contain NaN".
* Ordinary data no longer gives "RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in
  divide". The warning came from the last hull segment when it is horizontal.
  The computation drops that segment.

Changes

* Scores do not have to lie in [0,1]. EMP depends only on the order of the
  scores, so logits and scorecard points work. Scores that are NaN or infinite
  raise ValueError.
* Inputs that are not one-dimensional raise ValueError. A single-column pandas
  DataFrame and a row or column vector work. Version 2.0.4 flattened nested
  lists of any shape.
* The input checks use numpy operations instead of Python loops.
* The README now says that the functions return the output and do not print
  it by default.
* New tests in tests/. To run them, install pytest and run "python -m pytest"
  from the repository root.
